From 2f3fe2dc43b70af072865107497ce3b0d541b938 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hritik Utekar <hritikdrocks@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:24:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix window detection for apps reported with invalid PID (-1)

Some apps (e.g. Xcode 27 DeviceHub, launched via DevicesTrampoline) are
reported by LaunchServices with processIdentifier == -1. AXUIElementCreateApplication
and AXObserverCreate fail for such PIDs, so the app is never registered:
it is missing from list-apps/list-windows, debug-windows captures nothing,
and on-window-detected callbacks never fire.

Add NSRunningApplication.resolvedProcessIdentifier, which falls back to a
live process lookup (libproc executable-path match) when the reported PID
is invalid, and use it for app registration, AX element creation, observer
subscription, and app-map keys. Adds ResolvedPidTest coverage.
---
 Sources/AppBundle/tree/MacApp.swift           | 15 +++----
 Sources/AppBundle/util/AxSubscription.swift   |  4 +-
 .../util/NSRunningApplicationEx.swift         | 37 ++++++++++++++++++
 Sources/AppBundleTests/ResolvedPidTest.swift  | 39 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 86 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 Sources/AppBundleTests/ResolvedPidTest.swift

